Beamfall Core — Third-Party Notices (LB-3)
===========================================

This product includes software developed by third parties. The following
notices satisfy the attribution requirements of the MPL-2.0, BSD, MIT, and
Apache-2.0 licenses used by the dependencies listed below.

Source code and full license texts are available at the repository URLs shown.
This file covers dependencies bundled in non-container release tarballs; the
container image (Dockerfile) additionally incorporates an FFmpeg build
(GPL-3.0-or-later: --enable-gpl --enable-version3, no --enable-nonfree) and
the shared libraries it loads. It is FFmpeg 7.1.4 with the jellyfin-ffmpeg
v7.1.4-3 patch series (https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg), built by
tools/ffmpeg/build.sh against the Debian bookworm snapshot named in
internal/ffmpeg/ffmpeg.lock. It does not include the Fraunhofer FDK AAC
library or any other nonfree component; AAC is encoded with FFmpeg's native
encoder.

Written offer for the FFmpeg corresponding source (GPL-3.0 §6). For every
architecture the image ships (linux/amd64 and linux/arm64) it carries one
archive, /usr/share/beamfall/source/ffmpeg/
beamfall-ffmpeg-7.1.4-3-linux-<arch>-source.tar, with its SHA-256 in the
SHA256SUMS file beside it. The archive holds the locked upstream tarballs
(FFmpeg with its patch series, nv-codec-headers, AMD AMF headers), the
Debian source package (.dsc, upstream and Debian tarballs) of every library
the binaries load and of the bundled Intel VA-API, QSV and OpenCL runtimes,
each at the exact version installed, the build scripts, the lock, and
PACKAGES.txt listing each binary package and its source version. The GNU C
library and GCC runtime libraries are System Libraries and are not included.
A running server serves the archive to anyone, without sign-in, at
GET /source/ffmpeg, with its SHA-256 in the X-Checksum-SHA256 header.

